">USize</a>) → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">k</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/UInt/BasicAux.html#USize.toNat\">toNat</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LT.lt\">&lt;</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">len</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/UInt/BasicAux.html#USize.toNat\">toNat</a></span> → <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/SInt/Basic.html#Int64\">Int64</a> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">β</span> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/SInt/Basic.html#Int64\">Int64</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span></span></span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int64/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int64Array\">Int64Array</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <span class=\"fn\">β</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`foldlInPlace` on the slice `a[start.toNat...start.toNat + len.toNat]`, for bounds that are\nalready `USize`: returns the new array and the last accumulator. It is specified as that slice\nfold, so the slice lemmas apply after `foldlInPlaceRange_eq`. The implementation runs the loop of\n`foldlInPlace` on the `USize` bounds directly, without building the slice, whose `Nat` bounds\ncost a conversion on the way in and out of every call.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/Int64/InPlace.html#ScalarArray.Int64Array.foldlInPlaceRange","kind":"def","line":1128,"name":"ScalarArray.Int64Array.foldlInPlaceRange","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/ef15f198ef3e5fefe3f9b45b89a25772f75b1809/ScalarArray/Int64/InPlace.lean#L1128-L1143"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./ScalarArray/Int64/InPlace.html#ScalarArray.Int64Array.foldlInPlace2Then_eq_foldlInPlace2ThenImpl\"><span class=\"name\">ScalarArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">Int64Array</span>.<span class=\"name\">foldlInPlace2Then_eq_foldlInPlace2ThenImpl</span