\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">a'</span>.<a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int64/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int64Array.size\">size</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">a</span>.<a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int64/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int64Array.size\">size</a></span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">β</span> → <span class=\"fn\">γ</span></span></span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\">γ</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`foldlInPlace2` followed by `g` on the new array and the last accumulator, which the loop calls\nitself where `foldlInPlace2` returns them as a pair. When `g` consumes the accumulator, no pair is\nallocated. `g` also receives a proof that the size is unchanged, so that it can go on with bounded\nreads and writes, such as another `foldlInPlace2Then`.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/Int64/InPlace.html#ScalarArray.Int64Array.foldlInPlace2Then","kind":"def","line":1076,"name":"ScalarArray.Int64Array.foldlInPlace2Then","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/ef15f198ef3e5fefe3f9b45b89a25772f75b1809/ScalarArray/Int64/InPlace.lean#L1076-L1089"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./ScalarArray/Int64/InPlace.html#ScalarArray.Int64Array.foldlInPlace2_eq_foldlInPlace2Impl\"><span class=\"name\">ScalarArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">Int64Array</span>.<span class=\"name\">foldlInPlace2_eq_foldlInPlace2Impl</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\">@<a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int64/InPlace.html#ScalarArray.Int64Array.foldlInPlace2\">foldlInPlace2</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> @<a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int64/InPlace.html#ScalarArray.Int64Array.foldlInPlace2Impl\">foldlInPlace2Impl</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./ScalarArray/Int64/InPlace.html#ScalarArray.Int64Ar